#: data/io.github.sachesi.leyen.desktop:2
#: data/io.github.sachesi.leyen.metainfo.xml:6 ui/window.ui:46 ui/window.ui:57
msgid "Leyen"
msgstr "Leyen"

#: data/io.github.sachesi.leyen.desktop:3
msgid "Game Launcher"
msgstr "Запуск игр"

#: data/io.github.sachesi.leyen.desktop:10
msgid "wine;proton;umu;windows;"
msgstr "wine;proton;umu;windows;вайн;протон;виндовс;игры;"

#: data/io.github.sachesi.leyen.metainfo.xml:9
msgid ""
"Leyen keeps a library of Windows games and runs them with Proton through umu-"
"launcher, each in its own Wine prefix or in one shared with its group."
msgstr ""
"Leyen хранит библиотеку игр для Windows и запускает их через Proton с "
"помощью umu-launcher, каждую в собственном префиксе Wine или в общем для её "
"группы."

#: data/io.github.sachesi.leyen.metainfo.xml:11
msgid "Games in groups, with the playtime and the last session of each"
msgstr "Игры в группах, со временем в игре и последним сеансом каждой"

#: data/io.github.sachesi.leyen.metainfo.xml:12
msgid ""
"A Proton version, a prefix and launch arguments per game, or inherited from "
"the group and the defaults"
msgstr ""
"Версия Proton, префикс и аргументы запуска для каждой игры или "
"унаследованные от группы и параметров по умолчанию"

#: data/io.github.sachesi.leyen.metainfo.xml:13
msgid "MangoHud, Wayland, WoW64, NTSync and HDR switches"
msgstr "Переключатели MangoHud, Wayland, WoW64, NTSync и HDR"

#: data/io.github.sachesi.leyen.metainfo.xml:14
msgid ""
"Every game sandboxed: it reaches its prefix, its own folder and nothing else "
"of your files"
msgstr ""
"Каждая игра в песочнице: ей доступны свой префикс и собственная папка — и "
"больше ничего из ваших файлов"

#: data/io.github.sachesi.leyen.metainfo.xml:15
msgid ""
"Winetricks components, the Wine configuration and the registry editor for "
"any prefix"
msgstr ""
"Компоненты winetricks, настройка Wine и редактор реестра для любого префикса"

#: data/io.github.sachesi.leyen.metainfo.xml:16
msgid ""
"Menu entries that start a game from the desktop, and a command line to list, "
"run and stop games"
msgstr ""
"Пункты меню для запуска игры с рабочего стола и командная строка, чтобы "
"просматривать, запускать и останавливать игры"

#: data/io.github.sachesi.leyen.metainfo.xml:23
msgid "Keep every game in one library, on its own or in a group"
msgstr "Все игры в одной библиотеке — по отдельности или в группе"

#: data/io.github.sachesi.leyen.metainfo.xml:27
msgid "Open a group to reach the games that share its prefix and Proton"
msgstr "Откройте группу, чтобы добраться до игр с общим префиксом и Proton"

#: data/io.github.sachesi.leyen.metainfo.xml:31
msgid "Give a game its own Proton, prefix and launch arguments"
msgstr "Дайте игре свой Proton, префикс и аргументы запуска"

#: data/io.github.sachesi.leyen.metainfo.xml:35
msgid "Share a folder with a game, or cut it off from the network"
msgstr "Дайте игре доступ к ещё одной папке или отключите ей сеть"

#: data/io.github.sachesi.leyen.metainfo.xml:39
msgid "Install winetricks components into the prefix of a game"
msgstr "Устанавливайте компоненты winetricks в префикс игры"

#: data/io.github.sachesi.leyen.metainfo.xml:43
msgid "Set the prefix, the Proton and the switches every new game inherits"
msgstr ""
"Задайте префикс, Proton и переключатели, которые наследует каждая новая игра"

#: data/io.github.sachesi.leyen.metainfo.xml:61
msgid ""
"Every game runs in a sandbox now, and so does everything else that runs "
"Windows code: the Wine configuration, the registry editor, a program run by "
"hand and a dependency install. A program reaches its Wine prefix, the game "
"folder named in its settings and the folders shared with it, and nothing "
"else of your files; where the sandbox cannot be built, the launch is refused "
"instead of running unconfined. Two settings come with it, at the "
"preferences, the group and the game: extra folders to share, each read-only "
"unless switched writable, and network access."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.leyen.metainfo.xml:62
msgid ""
"Because the game folder is the one folder of yours a game sees, it is "
"required and set by hand, so games in a library from an earlier version need "
"it filled in before they launch again. GameMode is gone, switch and setting: "
"it cannot work from inside the sandbox, and keeping a game outside it would "
"let the game signal every program you run. bubblewrap and unprivileged user "
"namespaces are requirements from here on."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.leyen.metainfo.xml:63
msgid ""
"Games that share a prefix still share one wineserver, so three windows of "
"one game keep each other's registry writes. The Proton log is written into "
"the prefix, where it can be read after the game exits. The interface is "
"translated into Russian. On NixOS the sandbox builds and the prefix's "
"process namespace starts."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.leyen.metainfo.xml:68
msgid ""
"A dependency installed into a prefix that does not exist yet no longer "
"counts the whole Wine installation as its own files, so removing it, or a "
"failed install, leaves the prefix alone. Removing a component keeps the DLL "
"overrides another installed component set too, and removes the overrides "
"winetricks set, which were left behind. Reinstalling a winetricks component "
"works again, the first install waits for winetricks to finish downloading, "
"and the dependency manager waits for installs that take longer than five "
"minutes, such as .NET."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.leyen.metainfo.xml:69
msgid ""
"A failed download says why, and a failed installer ends its message with the "
"last lines of its output instead of all of it. A font installed again after "
"All Fonts keeps All Fonts from being removed before it. A group title with "
"an ampersand shows in the game dialog, and a menu entry is written only for "
"a game ID Leyen gave."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.leyen.metainfo.xml:74
msgid ""
"A launch whose first command cannot start, such as a wrapper in the launch "
"arguments that is not installed, no longer shows as running for good. "
"Stopping a game signals only that game's processes, even beside one with a "
"similar executable name on the same prefix, and a game's output keeps "
"reaching the log when it prints text that is not UTF-8."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.leyen.metainfo.xml:75
msgid ""
"Wine Configuration, the Registry Editor and programs run in a prefix are "
"tracked by the daemon: while they, or anything they started, run, no game "
"starts on that prefix and no dependency is installed or removed, and what "
"they print is in the log. Cancelling a dependency install stops every "
"process it started, Wine's server included. Installing dependencies needs "
"the systemd user session, as launching games does."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.leyen.metainfo.xml:76
msgid ""
"The umu-launcher and winetricks that Leyen downloads are releases pinned in "
"it, refused unless their SHA-256 matches. The log file is readable by you "
"alone, icons are read faster from executables that carry many images, and "
"editing a group updates its menu entries in one pass."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.leyen.metainfo.xml:81
msgid ""
"The window is rebuilt with GTK 4.22 and libadwaita 1.9. A group opens as a "
"page of its own that the back button, Escape or a swipe leave, and the "
"library is updated in place, so it no longer flickers or jumps when a game "
"starts or stops. Icons are larger and centred in their rows, and a logo on a "
"transparent background is shown whole instead of cropped. Search filters "
"what is loaded as it is typed and says when nothing matches, Enter launches "
"the game under the keyboard, and screen readers name every row. The log "
"follows new lines smoothly while it is at the end and stays where it was "
"scrolled to."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.leyen.metainfo.xml:82
msgid ""
"Adding and editing share one dialog for games and one for groups, which "
"cannot add the same game twice. The prefix tools are rows, the menu entry of "
"a game is a switch, and the dependency manager takes typing straight away, "
"clears it and then goes back on Escape, and says which components need the "
"one about to be removed. Deleting a group says how many games go with it, "
"and a game that is running cannot be deleted, nor a group with one running."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.leyen.metainfo.xml:83
msgid ""
"The application id is io.github.sachesi.leyen; icons and menu entries "
"written under the old id are moved over on the first start. Ctrl+Q quits, "
"Ctrl+W closes a window, and errors from the session bus read as a sentence "
"about the daemon. Installing no longer stops a daemon that is tracking "
"games, and the Ukrainian translation covers every new string of the "
"interface."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.leyen.metainfo.xml:88
msgid ""
"Winetricks components install again over an earlier attempt, removing one "
"takes it out of the prefix's record, catalogue entries run the verbs "
"winetricks knows them by, and DLL overrides are written to the registry "
"instead of only being noted. A game is told apart from its neighbours by its "
"GAMEID, a download that fails stops the others it was started with, and "
"runtimes are unpacked beside their destination before they replace it."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.leyen.metainfo.xml:89
msgid ""
"The window survives a restart of the daemon and no longer rebuilds the "
"library every few seconds while a game runs. The add and edit dialogs have a "
"title, and a group can be edited from the header while it is open."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.leyen.metainfo.xml:94
msgid ""
"Downloaded runtimes are checked against their digests and winetricks is "
"pinned to a known release. The files Leyen keeps carry a version of their "
"format, no more than four dependency jobs run at once, and a launch can no "
"longer slip in twice while the first is being registered. Menu entries of "
"games with the same name no longer overwrite each other, and a background "
"task that crashes no longer leaves the window waiting on it."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.leyen.metainfo.xml:99
msgid ""
"Files are read and written away from the thread drawing the window. A "
"dependency job and a launch no longer run against the same prefix at once, a "
"session is removed only once its playtime is saved, and \"leyen list\" shows "
"a running game that is no longer in the library."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.leyen.metainfo.xml:104
msgid "The library keeps its scroll position when it is refreshed."
msgstr "Библиотека сохраняет позицию прокрутки при обновлении."

#: data/io.github.sachesi.leyen.metainfo.xml:109
msgid ""
"Games are started and tracked by a daemon on the session bus, which the "
"window and the command line talk to. It exits when it has nothing to do, "
"writes the library and the settings so that a crash cannot leave them half "
"written, and reports why an operation failed. Dependency downloads can be "
"cancelled, and the log window follows new lines as they come."
msgstr ""

